- validateMileageMiles('12.5') returns null.
- validateMileageMiles('12.55') returns 'Miles can have at most 1 decimal place'.

Also earlier tests: __tests__/acceptance/m5.test.ts includes validateMileageMiles in numeric validation:

```
it('validates mileage miles correctly', () => {
    expect(validateMileageMiles(0)).toBe('Miles must be > 0');
    expect(validateMileageMiles(-10)).toBe('Miles must be > 0');
    expect(validateMileageMiles(10001)).toBe('Miles must be ≤ 10,000');
    expect(validateMileageMiles(250)).toBeNull();
});
```

The test expects errors for 0, negative, >10000, null for 250. It doesn't test string representation of non-numeric.

