{
  "summary": "Overall the app implements the complete primary flow, all required screens, and most of the specified states. The UI uses the Material‑3 theme, respects the 44 × 44 dp touch‑target rule, and the automated axe audit reports zero accessibility violations. Navigation from any signed‑in screen to the main actions (add receipt/mileage, settings, export, backup) works via the persistent bottom‑tab bar and FAB. However a handful of spec‑level details are missing or only partially implemented: a few secondary error states are not present, some accessibility affordances (focus outlines, ARIA roles, image alt text) are omitted, and a couple of design‑token usages fall back to hard‑coded values. These issues are low‑to‑medium severity and can be fixed without breaking the primary flow.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The error state for the PolicyGate (when storing acceptance fails) is not rendered – there is no full‑screen error view with the copy “Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.” and a Retry button.",
      "fix": "Add an error UI branch that displays the specified message and a Retry button that re‑attempts the storage operation. Use the theme’s error color for text."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Dashboard lacks a dedicated loading state; when the app first loads data there is no centered ActivityIndicator as described in the spec.",
      "fix": "Introduce a loading flag in the dashboard logic and render a centered `<ActivityIndicator size=\"large\" />` while receipts/mileage are being fetched from the store."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/OfflineBanner.tsx",
      "issue": "The full‑screen offline indicator (copy “You are offline. Some actions require an internet connection.”) is not present in any screen, so users receive no feedback when the network is unavailable.",
      "fix": "Create an `OfflineBanner` component that subscribes to network status and displays the banner at the top of the screen when offline. Include it in the `Screen` wrapper so it appears on every screen."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/MiniFAB.tsx",
      "issue": "Mini‑FABs for “Add receipt” and “Add mileage” lack `accessibilityLabel` props, so screen‑readers cannot announce their purpose.",
      "fix": "Pass `accessibilityLabel=\"Add receipt\"` and `accessibilityLabel=\"Add mileage\"` (or appropriate strings) to the `FAB` components."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Focus‑visible outline is not applied; on focus the button shows only the default ripple, missing the required 2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline`.",
      "fix": "Add a style rule for `:focus-visible` (or the React Native `onFocus` state) that sets `borderWidth: 2` and `borderColor: theme.colors.outline`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The “Delete all data” row is not preceded by a `<Divider />` and does not explicitly use the `error` color from the design tokens.",
      "fix": "Insert a `<Divider />` component before the Delete row and set its text color to `theme.colors.error` (or the `error` variant on the `List.Item`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/CategoriesScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The Add Category dialog uses a generic title and label rather than the exact copy “Add new category” and “Category name”.",
      "fix": "Update the `<Dialog.Title>` and `<TextInput label>` props to match the required copy exactly."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Miles field validation does not enforce the “max 1 decimal place” rule; users can enter values like 12.55 without error.",
      "fix": "Add regex validation (e.g., `/^\\d+(\\.\\d)?$/`) in the validation layer and display the HelperText error “Miles can have at most 1 decimal place”."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The OCR‑no‑data alert dialog shows a generic message instead of the required copy “No details could be extracted – please enter manually.”",
      "fix": "Replace the alert text with the exact copy from the spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "On web the FAB tool‑tip for the Scan button (“Scanning is available in the phone app”) is not rendered.",
      "fix": "Wrap the Scan FAB with a `<Tooltip>` component that displays the specified tooltip only on non‑mobile platforms."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/* (any component with static color values)",
      "issue": "Several components use hard‑coded hex colour values (e.g., `#0061A4`) instead of referencing the theme tokens (`theme.colors.primary`).",
      "fix": "Replace all literal colour strings with references to the appropriate design token from `src/theme.ts`."
    }
  ]
}

